{{!--
  Dragonbane — the front of every card type but generic.

  One front template, not one per card type. It renders a fixed set of
  PLACES, each named after where it sits on the card, never after what a
  particular card type puts there:

      front-header-title        the title on the plaque
      front-header-die          the die hanging off the plaque's lower right
      front-header-subtitle     the small tag on the plaque's lower left
      front-image-top / -bottom the illustration, above or below the body
      front-stat-1a … 8c        the stat box's short cells, by row and column
      front-stat-1-wide … 8        a stat row given over to one wrapping value
      front-stat-1-wide-tail … 8   a short value trailing that wide row
      front-stat-list           trailing labelled rows built from a data list
      front-trait-list          the same shape of list, as ONE unruled block
      front-table               a caption line plus a roll/name/desc table
      front-detail-text         a block shown only in the detailed display mode
      front-text-top   / -bottom    prose above / below the stat box
      front-effect-top / -bottom    prose carrying the "Effekt" label
      front-note-top   / -bottom    quiet italic afterword
      front-side-left  / -right     the two rotated edge labels

  A card type fills a place by naming it on one of its properties in
  dragonbane.yaml (`grip: { slot: front-stat-1a }`) and captions it in its
  translations (`front-stat-1a-label: "Griff"`). A place the card type does
  not fill has no value and renders nothing — which is how one template
  serves a weapon and a roll-table row without a single branch on the card
  type. How a place renders is said here, on the call: the stat cells are
  `markdown=false` (a value shows its link styled and nothing else), the
  prose is markdown, the two titles are `plain=true` for the FontScaler.

  The stat box is eight rows, each either up to three short cells or one
  wide wrapping value with an optional short tail. What repeats is the
  markup, not the decision, so a cell and a wide row are each one partial:

      {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-1a"}}
      {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-1-wide" tail="front-stat-1-wide-tail"}}

  The row structure stays here: the `{{#if …-wide}} … {{else if …a/b/c}}`
  decides whether a row is wide or three cells, and that is the arrangement
  of the card, which belongs visibly here.

  The blocks appear in ONE fixed DOM order for every card type. That is a
  requirement, not a simplification: the overflow splitter paginates by DOM
  order, so reordering the body per card type with CSS `order` would break
  every card that runs onto a second face. Where two card types genuinely
  disagree about position, the place exists TWICE — `front-text-top` above
  the stat box, `front-text-bottom` below it — and each card type fills the
  one it wants.

  The three spacers (`.db-fill-top`, `-mid`, `-bottom`) are always in the
  markup; a card type's stylesheet gives each the flex weight its vertical
  rhythm wants, or none. They are left out when the card has an
  illustration: `.db-front-image-wrap` is itself a `flex: 1 1 0` slot and
  would lose its room to them.
--}}
<div class="card-root card-front dragonbane {{card-type}}-card">
  <div class="db-head">
    <div class="db-title-plaque">
      {{#if (slot "front-header-die")}}
      <span class="roll-table-badge"><span class="roll-table-badge-num roll-table-badge-num-{{slot-class "front-header-die"}}">{{slot "front-header-die" markdown=false}}</span></span>
      {{/if}}

      {{!-- The subtitle tag mirrors the die on the opposite edge. Suppressed
            when it would only repeat the title — `front-header-title` falls
            back to the note's basename, so a table whose rows carry no names
            of their own titles every card "FURCHT", and a tag reading FURCHT
            hanging off a plaque reading FURCHT is a mistake, not a label. --}}
      {{#if (slot "front-header-subtitle")}}
      {{#unless (eq (slot "front-header-title" plain=true) (slot "front-header-subtitle" plain=true))}}
      <span class="roll-table-category roll-table-category-{{slot-class "front-header-subtitle"}}"><span class="roll-table-category-text">{{slot "front-header-subtitle" markdown=false}}</span></span>
      {{/unless}}
      {{/if}}

      <div class="card-title"><span class="text-scalable">{{slot "front-header-title" plain=true}}</span></div>
      <span class="cf-overflow-counter"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="db-strip db-strip-top"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card-content-container">
    <div class="card-body-scalable">

    {{#if (slot "front-lead-text")}}
    <p class="db-flavor">{{slot "front-lead-text"}}</p>
    {{/if}}

    {{#unless (or (slot "front-image-top") (slot "front-image-bottom"))}}
    <span class="db-fill-top"></span>
    {{/unless}}

    {{!-- The same partial the engine renders every `![[bild.png]]` of a
          note body through — see card-image.hbs. --}}
    {{#if (slot "front-image-top")}}
    {{> card-image url=(slot "front-image-top" image=true) alt="" placement="front"}}
    {{/if}}

    {{#if (or (slot "front-text-top") (slot "front-effect-top") (slot "front-note-top"))}}
    <div class="db-effect-block db-effect-block-top">
      {{#if (slot "front-text-top")}}
      <p class="db-effect-text">{{slot "front-text-top"}}</p>
      {{/if}}
      {{#if (slot "front-effect-top")}}
      <p class="db-effect-text"><span class="db-effect-label">{{t "effect-label"}}</span>{{slot "front-effect-top"}}</p>
      {{/if}}
      {{#if (slot "front-note-top")}}
      <p class="db-effect-text"><em>{{slot "front-note-top"}}</em></p>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- ── The stat box ────────────────────────────────────────────────
          Eight rows, each either up to three short nowrap cells (`.db-stat`)
          or one wrapping free-text value (`.db-stats-row-wide`). A row is
          wide exactly when the card type fills its `-wide` place instead of
          its a/b/c cells — nothing extra to declare. --}}
    {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-1a") (slot "front-stat-1b") (slot "front-stat-1c") (slot "front-stat-1-wide") (slot "front-stat-1-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-2a") (slot "front-stat-2b") (slot "front-stat-2c") (slot "front-stat-2-wide") (slot "front-stat-2-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-3a") (slot "front-stat-3b") (slot "front-stat-3c") (slot "front-stat-3-wide") (slot "front-stat-3-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-4a") (slot "front-stat-4b") (slot "front-stat-4c") (slot "front-stat-4-wide") (slot "front-stat-4-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-5a") (slot "front-stat-5b") (slot "front-stat-5c") (slot "front-stat-5-wide") (slot "front-stat-5-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-6a") (slot "front-stat-6b") (slot "front-stat-6c") (slot "front-stat-6-wide") (slot "front-stat-6-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-7a") (slot "front-stat-7b") (slot "front-stat-7c") (slot "front-stat-7-wide") (slot "front-stat-7-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-8a") (slot "front-stat-8b") (slot "front-stat-8c") (slot "front-stat-8-wide") (slot "front-stat-8-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-list" list=true) (slot "front-trait-list" list=true))}}
    <div class="db-stats-box">
      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-1-wide") (slot "front-stat-1-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-1-wide" tail="front-stat-1-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-1a") (slot "front-stat-1b") (slot "front-stat-1c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-1a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-1b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-1c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-2-wide") (slot "front-stat-2-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-2-wide" tail="front-stat-2-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-2a") (slot "front-stat-2b") (slot "front-stat-2c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-2a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-2b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-2c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-3-wide") (slot "front-stat-3-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-3-wide" tail="front-stat-3-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-3a") (slot "front-stat-3b") (slot "front-stat-3c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-3a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-3b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-3c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-4-wide") (slot "front-stat-4-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-4-wide" tail="front-stat-4-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-4a") (slot "front-stat-4b") (slot "front-stat-4c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-4a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-4b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-4c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-5-wide") (slot "front-stat-5-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-5-wide" tail="front-stat-5-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-5a") (slot "front-stat-5b") (slot "front-stat-5c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-5a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-5b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-5c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-6-wide") (slot "front-stat-6-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-6-wide" tail="front-stat-6-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-6a") (slot "front-stat-6b") (slot "front-stat-6c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-6a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-6b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-6c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-7-wide") (slot "front-stat-7-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-7-wide" tail="front-stat-7-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-7a") (slot "front-stat-7b") (slot "front-stat-7c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-7a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-7b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-7c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-8-wide") (slot "front-stat-8-wide-tail"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        {{> stat-wide for="front-stat-8-wide" tail="front-stat-8-wide-tail"}}
      </div>
      {{else if (or (slot "front-stat-8a") (slot "front-stat-8b") (slot "front-stat-8c"))}}
      <div class="db-stats-row">
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-8a"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-8b"}}
        {{> stat-cell for="front-stat-8c"}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}

      {{!-- Rows the card carries as DATA rather than as fixed places: a list
            of {name, desc} pairs, each set as one wide row. This is how a
            table whose columns differ per table (Rationen, Voraussetzungen,
            Heilungsdauer) reaches the same stat box as a fixed card type. --}}
      {{#each (slot "front-stat-list" list=true)}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-wide">
        <p class="db-trait"><span class="db-trait-name">{{name}}</span>{{desc}}</p>
      </div>
      {{/each}}

      {{!-- The same {name, desc} shape as `front-stat-list`, set as ONE row
            instead of one row per item. The difference is the rule between
            rows, and it is the whole point of having two places: a table
            row's values ("Rationen: 2W6") read as a table and want the rules,
            while a creature's traits ("Regeneration: Ein Troll heilt …") are
            prose paragraphs that the same rules would chop up. --}}
      {{#if (slot "front-trait-list" list=true)}}
      <div class="db-stats-row db-stats-row-traits">
        {{#each (slot "front-trait-list" list=true)}}
        <p class="db-trait"><span class="db-trait-name">{{name}}</span>{{desc}}</p>
        {{/each}}
      </div>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- A captioned roll/name/description table — the Monsterangriffe. Its
          items carry `roll`, `name` and `desc`; the caption and the two column
          heads come from the card type's translations, like every other label.

          The caption is `.db-section-heading`, the plain centred caps line,
          NOT a `.db-plaque-strip`: the heading belongs to the table under it
          and its margins are asymmetric for exactly that reason, while a
          plaque reads as a component in its own right.

          Heading and table are two top-level blocks, so the splitter is free
          to cut between them. It takes BOTH of the following to keep them
          together, and they cover two different paths — removing either one
          strands the heading on one of them, so do not "simplify" this.

          The table breaks between rows by default — the common path. A table
          paginates between the `<tr>`s of its `<tbody>`, and the `<thead>` is
          repeated on the continuation so the tail keeps its column labels. The
          heading then belongs to the fitting PREFIX and the table surrenders
          only the rows that have no room.

          `cf-keep-with-next` on the heading — the remaining path. When not even
          ONE row fits beside the prefix, the whole table moves on, which would
          leave the heading behind as the last block; the marker pulls the
          heading along with it. It is a no-op when the heading is block 0 of a
          continuation face, and without a splittable table it would merely drag
          the heading off a face it fitted on — with the table splittable it
          fires only where it is right. --}}
    {{#if (slot "front-table" list=true)}}
    {{#if (slot-label "front-table")}}
    <div class="db-section-heading cf-keep-with-next">{{slot-label "front-table"}}</div>
    {{/if}}
    <table class="db-attack-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="db-attack-th-roll">{{t "front-table-col-1-label"}}</th>
          <th class="db-attack-th-name">{{t "front-table-col-2-label"}}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {{#each (slot "front-table" list=true)}}
        <tr>
          <td class="db-attack-roll">{{roll}}</td>
          <td class="db-attack-cell"><span class="db-attack-name">{{name}}</span>{{desc}}</td>
        </tr>
        {{/each}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- The middle spacer — only with something on BOTH sides of it,
          otherwise its share would open a hole in an arbitrary place. Nested
          rather than one condition: there is `or` but no `and`. --}}
    {{#unless (or (slot "front-image-top") (slot "front-image-bottom"))}}
    {{#if (or (slot "front-stat-1a") (slot "front-stat-1b") (slot "front-stat-1c") (slot "front-stat-1-wide") (slot "front-stat-1-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-2a") (slot "front-stat-2b") (slot "front-stat-2c") (slot "front-stat-2-wide") (slot "front-stat-2-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-3a") (slot "front-stat-3b") (slot "front-stat-3c") (slot "front-stat-3-wide") (slot "front-stat-3-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-4a") (slot "front-stat-4b") (slot "front-stat-4c") (slot "front-stat-4-wide") (slot "front-stat-4-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-5a") (slot "front-stat-5b") (slot "front-stat-5c") (slot "front-stat-5-wide") (slot "front-stat-5-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-6a") (slot "front-stat-6b") (slot "front-stat-6c") (slot "front-stat-6-wide") (slot "front-stat-6-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-7a") (slot "front-stat-7b") (slot "front-stat-7c") (slot "front-stat-7-wide") (slot "front-stat-7-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-8a") (slot "front-stat-8b") (slot "front-stat-8c") (slot "front-stat-8-wide") (slot "front-stat-8-wide-tail")
              (slot "front-stat-list" list=true) (slot "front-trait-list" list=true))}}
    {{#if (or (slot "front-text-bottom") (slot "front-effect-bottom") (slot "front-note-bottom"))}}
    <span class="db-fill-mid"></span>
    {{/if}}
    {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}

    {{#if (or (slot "front-text-bottom") (slot "front-effect-bottom") (slot "front-note-bottom"))}}
    <div class="db-effect-block db-effect-block-bottom">
      {{#if (slot "front-text-bottom")}}
      <p class="db-effect-text">{{slot "front-text-bottom"}}</p>
      {{/if}}
      {{#if (slot "front-effect-bottom")}}
      <p class="db-effect-text"><span class="db-effect-label">{{t "effect-label"}}</span>{{slot "front-effect-bottom"}}</p>
      {{/if}}
      {{#if (slot "front-note-bottom")}}
      <p class="db-effect-text"><em>{{slot "front-note-bottom"}}</em></p>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- GM-only material: hidden by default, revealed only in the "detailed"
          display mode, which stamps `.cf-detailed` on `.card-root`. The card
          type's CSS owns that gate; the place only supplies the text. --}}
    {{#if (slot "front-detail-text")}}
    <div class="db-gm-note">
      {{#if (slot-label "front-detail-text")}}<span class="db-gm-note-label">{{slot-label "front-detail-text"}}</span>{{/if}}
      {{slot "front-detail-text"}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- The illustration again, at the FOOT of the body. A card type fills
          either this or `front-image-top`, never both: the picture is one
          picture, and which end of the card it belongs at is exactly the sort
          of decision a place's name is supposed to carry. The creature
          cards lead with their stat block and close with the portrait; the
          gear and rule cards lead with the picture. --}}
    {{#if (slot "front-image-bottom")}}
    {{> card-image url=(slot "front-image-bottom" image=true) alt="" placement="front"}}
    {{/if}}

    {{#unless (or (slot "front-image-top") (slot "front-image-bottom"))}}
    <span class="db-fill-bottom"></span>
    {{/unless}}

    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="db-strip db-strip-bottom"></div>

  {{!-- The two edge labels, a mirrored pair. Both are absolutely positioned,
        i.e. OUT of the flex flow, so neither costs the body a single line. The
        left one appears only when a card type fills it; the right one falls
        back to "DRAGONBANE". --}}
  {{#if (slot "front-side-left")}}
  <div class="db-side-english">{{#if (slot-label "front-side-left")}}<span class="db-side-english-label">{{slot-label "front-side-left"}}</span>{{/if}}{{slot "front-side-left" markdown=false}}</div>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="db-side-ref">{{slot "front-side-right" markdown=false fallback=(t "side-ref")}}</div>

  {{!-- "Geht weiter" — an arrowhead in the right-hand gutter, above the bottom
        ornament. Hidden by default; the stylesheet reveals it under the
        splitter's `.cf-front-has-next`, i.e. on every front face EXCEPT the
        last. Absolutely positioned like the edge labels, so it costs the body
        nothing and cannot clip.

        Only on the front. `back.hbs` is a different construction and its face
        never continues: a card that fits keeps its designed back, and one that
        overflows has that back replaced by a CLONE of this front, which brings
        the arrow with it. --}}
  <div class="db-cont-arrow"></div>
</div>
